@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `nii-il06-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il06-period`
IMPORT `nii-s1-basic-amount`
IMPORT `nii-s65-interpretation`
IMPORT `nii-s66-entitlement`
IMPORT `nii-s67-count-of-children`
IMPORT `nii-s68-amount`
IMPORT `nii-il06-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-il06-family-on-a-day`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-06: National Insurance Law ss 65-68.
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-06's modules, and no other row.
-- Exposes numbers and booleans. IL-06's `A child` and `A problem with the facts`
-- share their names with types of rows IL-02 and IL-03 (RECONCILE.md, clashes
-- N3 and N4); here they are IL-06's.
--
-- WHICH DAY. IL-06 answers a family on a day, at the basic amounts in force that
-- day; s 72 (which months are paid) is not encoded (IL-06 NOTES.md section 2).
-- The capstone asks on the FIRST day of the month, and declines a month in which
-- a child of the household is born or turns 18 after that day (NOTES.md fork
-- K6): in every other month nothing IL-06 reads changes during the month for a
-- household of the capstone's shape (the basic amounts change on 1 January).
--
-- THE FAMILY AS IL-06 SEES IT (input conventions, BRIEF.md "The household"):
-- * the earner is not a housewife: NII s 238 (source line 2428) defines one as a
--   married woman "שאינה עובדת ואינה עובדת עצמאית", and the earner is employed;
-- * nobody is absent from Israel, formerly insured, paid Income Support or a
--   maintenance payment, or (for s 69A) a man with children by more than one
--   woman; no child is married or abroad;
-- * every child is the natural child of the earner and of the spouse if any,
--   and is with each of them.
-- A child born after the day is not yet in the family on that day and is left
-- out of it (row IL-06 would otherwise report a problem with the facts).
--
-- VERSION 0.2.0 SUPERSEDES "WHICH DAY": row IL-08 encodes s 72, and the pipeline
-- asks IL-06 about the children s 72 pays for in the month, on a day on which
-- IL-06 counts every one of them (NOTES.md fork K15), through
-- `IL-06: the child allowance on ... , for the children ...` below. The 0.1.0
-- rule that declined a month with a birth or an 18th birthday after the 1st is
-- removed (it also let an 18th birthday ON the 1st through as 0: independent
-- finding F3). The first-day rules remain for the tests of IL-06's own period.
-- A problem with the facts now becomes a refusal that says what it is where the
-- household can cause it (independent finding M1).
--
-- VERSION 0.3.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-22) SUPERSEDES the day of fork K15. Row
-- IL-06's version 0.2.0 answers a MONTH for the children the caller says s 72
-- pays for in it (its 06-S72): `A family in a month`, and `the child allowance of
-- each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, at the basic
-- amounts the Institute published for the month, in`. Its s 65 age limb is then
-- met for the month by a listed child whose 18th birthday is on or after the
-- month's first day and who is born by its last. The pipeline now asks that,
-- through `IL-06: the child allowance for the month, in ... , for the children
-- section 72 pays for ...` below, with the children row IL-08's s 72 pays for;
-- no day is chosen and none is declined. The day forms remain for the tests.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-06`

§§ `The day`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A DATE
`IL-06: the first day of the month, in` h MEANS
    YMD (h's `the year of the month`) (h's `the month of the year`) 1

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A DATE
`IL-06: the last day of the month, in` h MEANS
    YMD (h's `the year of the month`) (h's `the month of the year`) (`Days in month` (h's `the month of the year`) (h's `the year of the month`))

§§ `The household, as IL-06's family on a day`

GIVEN `is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Father or mother`
`IL-06: father or mother` `is a woman` MEANS
    IF `is a woman` THEN `the child's mother` ELSE `the child's father`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person`
`IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    `A person` WITH
        `name`                                                                                       IS e's `the earner's name`
        `insured under Chapter 11`                                                                   IS e's `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`
        `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                                      IS FALSE
        `resident in Israel`                                                                         IS e's `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`
        `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`                                  IS FALSE
        `formerly insured`                                                                           IS FALSE
        `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`        IS `chargeable to additional tax`
        `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`                               IS FALSE
        `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law`   IS FALSE
        `children by more than one woman`                                                            IS FALSE
    WHERE
        e MEANS h's `the earner`

-- The spouse has no income (the pipeline declines otherwise), so no income
-- chargeable to additional tax.
GIVEN c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `A person`
`IL-06: the spouse as a person, in` c MEANS
    `A person` WITH
        `name`                                                                                       IS s's `the spouse's name`
        `insured under Chapter 11`                                                                   IS s's `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`
        `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                                      IS s's `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law`
        `resident in Israel`                                                                         IS s's `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`
        `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`                                  IS FALSE
        `formerly insured`                                                                           IS FALSE
        `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`        IS FALSE
        `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`                               IS FALSE
        `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law`   IS FALSE
        `children by more than one woman`                                                            IS FALSE
    WHERE
        s MEANS c's `the earner's spouse`

GIVEN `the name`   IS A STRING
      `is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`IL-06: the natural parent` `the name` `, a woman:` `is a woman` `, with whom the child is` MEANS
    `A parent in a child's record` WITH
        `name of the person`            IS `the name`
        `standing`                      IS `the child's natural parent`
        `father or mother`              IS `IL-06: father or mother` `is a woman`
        `the child is with this person` IS TRUE
        `support proven`                IS FALSE

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      k IS AN `IL-07 child`
GIVETH A `A child`
`IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k MEANS
    `A child` WITH
        `name`                                           IS k's `the child's name`
        `date of birth`                                  IS k's `the child's date of birth`
        `married`                                        IS FALSE
        `absence from Israel`                            IS NOTHING
        `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`   IS FALSE
        `parents`                                        IS `the earner's entry` FOLLOWED BY `the spouse's entries`
    WHERE
        e MEANS h's `the earner`
        `the earner's entry` MEANS `IL-06: the natural parent` (e's `the earner's name`) `, a woman:` (e's `the earner is a woman`) `, with whom the child is`
        `the spouse's entries` MEANS
            CONSIDER h's `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST c  THEN LIST `IL-06: the natural parent` (c's `the earner's spouse`'s `the spouse's name`) `, a woman:` (c's `the earner's spouse`'s `the spouse is a woman`) `, with whom the child is`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`IL-06: the family on the first day of the month, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    `A family on a day` WITH
        `the day`      IS `the day`
        `the persons`  IS `the earner` FOLLOWED BY `the spouse`
        `the children` IS map (GIVEN k YIELD `IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k)
                              (filter (GIVEN k YIELD k's `the child's date of birth` AT MOST `the day`) (h's `the children of the household`))
    WHERE
        `the day`    MEANS `IL-06: the first day of the month, in` h
        `the earner` MEANS `IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`
        `the spouse` MEANS
            CONSIDER h's `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST c  THEN LIST `IL-06: the spouse as a person, in` c

§§ `The 18th birthday, as row IL-06 reckons it`

-- IL-06's own anniversary rule (its fork F2: a birth on 29 February has its
-- anniversary on 28 February in a common year), which the pipeline passes to
-- row IL-08's s 72 as the day entitlement ceases.
@ref NII s 65 "ילד" proviso (row IL-06, nii-s65-interpretation.l4)
GIVEN k IS AN `IL-07 child`
      h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A DATE
`IL-06: the 18th birthday of` k `, in` h MEANS
    `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` (`IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k)

-- VERSION 0.4.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-44). Row IL-06's version 0.3.0 (its fork F2,
-- ruled SHRUG) declines the rule above for a child born on 29 February: eighteen
-- years on is never a leap year, and the Law does not say whether the period ends on
-- 28 February or on 1 March. That would decline every month for such a child. The
-- pipeline therefore asks row IL-08's s 72 at each of IL-06's two other readings,
-- through the two rules below, and declines, in IL-06's words, only a month whose
-- answer differs (the month after February of the 18th year). For any other child
-- the two days are one.
@ref NII s 65 "ילד" proviso (row IL-06 v0.3.0, nii-s65-interpretation.l4, fork F2)
GIVEN k IS AN `IL-07 child`
      h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A DATE
`IL-06: the 18th birthday of` k `, in` h `, a missing day clamped to the last day of the shorter month` MEANS
    `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` (`IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k)
        `, reading a missing day as` `a missing day clamps to the last day of the shorter month`

@ref NII s 65 "ילד" proviso (row IL-06 v0.3.0, nii-s65-interpretation.l4, fork F2)
GIVEN k IS AN `IL-07 child`
      h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A DATE
`IL-06: the 18th birthday of` k `, in` h `, a missing day rolled to the 1st of the next month` MEANS
    `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` (`IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k)
        `, reading a missing day as` `a missing day rolls to the 1st of the next month`

-- IL-06's refusal for fork F2, in its own words, for the pipeline to use.
@ref NII s 65 "ילד" proviso (row IL-06 v0.3.0, nii-s65-interpretation.l4, fork F2)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-06: the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks` MEANS
    `the Law does not say on which day a period ends that would end on a day the later month lacks, such as 29 February in a common year`

@ref NII s 65 "ילד" proviso (row IL-06, nii-s65-interpretation.l4)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      h         IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      k         IS AN `IL-07 child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-06: under 18 on` `the day` `, in` h `:` k MEANS
    `s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` (`IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k)

§§ `The child allowance`

-- A problem with the facts, as a refusal that says what it is (independent
-- finding M1). The other three cannot arise from a household record: the
-- adapter names every parent among the persons, leaves out a child not yet
-- born, and gives no absence. (Version 0.3.0: row IL-06's version 0.2.0 added
-- three: a finished absence, which the adapter cannot give; and a child said to
-- be paid for in the month who is born after it, or 18 before it began, which
-- the pipeline cannot give either, because it lists only the children row
-- IL-08's s 72 pays for, with the 18th birthday as row IL-06 reckons it. They
-- reach the general refusal below if they ever arise.)
GIVEN p IS A `A problem with the facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the refusal for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `two children have the same name`
        THEN `two children of the household have the same name; row IL-06 tells children apart by name, so give each child a name of its own`
    WHEN `two persons have the same name`
        THEN `the earner and the spouse have the same name; row IL-06 tells the persons of a family apart by name, so give each a name of their own`
    OTHERWISE `IL-06 reports that the household's facts cannot describe a family on the day`

@ref NII ss 65-68 (row IL-06, nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4), at the basic amounts the Institute published (nii-il06-published-figures.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the household's child allowance for the month, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` `the family`
    WHEN LEFT  p           THEN `IL-06: the refusal for` p
    WHEN RIGHT `the answers` THEN `the family's total, before rounding, of` `the answers`
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS `IL-06: the family on the first day of the month, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`

-- Version 0.2.0: the family on a day the caller names, with the children the
-- caller names (those s 72 pays for in the month; the pipeline chooses a day on
-- which IL-06 counts each of them).
GIVEN `the day`      IS A DATE
      h              IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the children` IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`IL-06: the family on` `the day` `, in` h `, with the children` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    `A family on a day` WITH
        `the day`      IS `the day`
        `the persons`  IS `the earner` FOLLOWED BY `the spouse`
        `the children` IS map (GIVEN k YIELD `IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k) `the children`
    WHERE
        `the earner` MEANS `IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`
        `the spouse` MEANS
            CONSIDER h's `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST c  THEN LIST `IL-06: the spouse as a person, in` c

@ref NII ss 65-68 (row IL-06, nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4), at the basic amounts the Institute published (nii-il06-published-figures.l4)
GIVEN `the day`      IS A DATE
      h              IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the children` IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the child allowance on` `the day` `, in` h `, for the children` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` `the family`
    WHEN LEFT  p             THEN `IL-06: the refusal for` p
    WHEN RIGHT `the answers` THEN `the family's total, before rounding, of` `the answers`
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS `IL-06: the family on` `the day` `, in` h `, with the children` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`

-- Version 0.3.0: the household as row IL-06's family in a month. The day on
-- which the facts stand is the month's first: every fact this record reads, but
-- the children's dates of birth, is the same on each day of the month for a
-- household of the capstone's shape (the basic amounts change on 1 January). The
-- children are those the caller says s 72 pays for in the month (the pipeline:
-- row IL-08's s 72).
@ref NII ss 65-68 with s 72(a) as the caller applies it (row IL-06 v0.2.0, nii-il06-nouns.l4, `A family in a month`)
GIVEN h              IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the children` IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A family in a month`
`IL-06: the family in the month, in` h `, with the children section 72 pays for` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    `A family in a month` WITH
        `a day in the month, on which the facts stand`  IS `IL-06: the first day of the month, in` h
        `the persons`                                   IS `the earner` FOLLOWED BY `the spouse`
        `the children section 72 pays for in the month` IS map (GIVEN k YIELD `IL-06: the household's child, in` h `:` k) `the children`
    WHERE
        `the earner` MEANS `IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`
        `the spouse` MEANS
            CONSIDER h's `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST c  THEN LIST `IL-06: the spouse as a person, in` c

@ref NII ss 65-68, s 72(a) as the caller applies it (row IL-06 v0.2.0, nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4), at the basic amounts the Institute published (nii-il06-published-figures.l4)
GIVEN h              IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the children` IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the child allowance for the month, in` h `, for the children section 72 pays for` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the child allowance of each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the month, in` `the family`
    WHEN LEFT  p             THEN `IL-06: the refusal for` p
    WHEN RIGHT `the answers` THEN `the family's total, before rounding, of` `the answers`
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS `IL-06: the family in the month, in` h `, with the children section 72 pays for` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`

-- For the tests: how many children IL-06's s 67 counts with the earner, and with
-- the spouse.
@ref NII s 67 (row IL-06, nii-s67-count-of-children.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the number of children in the earner's count, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    count (`s 67 — the count of children, in` `the family` `, of` (`IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`))
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS `IL-06: the family on the first day of the month, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`

-- Version 0.5.0: row IL-06's version 0.4.0 makes its fork F6 a switch (SHRUG): a
-- child whose insured parent s 66 excludes stays in that parent's count, or goes
-- to another insured parent's, and by default the case is declined where the two
-- part. The capstone names F6's reading (il07-nouns.l4); every other fork of row
-- IL-06 stays at its own switch. A household of the capstone's shape reaches F6
-- where the earner is a father with income chargeable to additional tax and the
-- mother is a resident s 238 housewife (row IL-06's NOTES.md, "For the capstone").
@ref NII ss 66, 67(b) (row IL-06 v0.4.0, nii-s65-interpretation.l4, its fork F6)
GIVEN x IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the count of a parent excluded by section 66`
GIVETH A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
`IL-06: its readings, with the count of an excluded parent read as` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `IL-07: the count of an excluded parent at row IL-06's switch, declined where the readings differ` THEN `the readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
    WHEN `IL-07: the child stays in the count of the parent section 66 excludes`                            THEN `the readings this row takes where the text does not decide` `with the count of an excluded parent read as` `the child stays in the excluded parent's count`
    WHEN `IL-07: the child goes to the count of another insured parent, not excluded`                       THEN `the readings this row takes where the text does not decide` `with the count of an excluded parent read as` `the child goes to the count of another insured parent who is not excluded`

@ref NII ss 65-68, s 72(a) as the caller applies it (row IL-06 v0.4.0, nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4, its fork F6), at the basic amounts the Institute published (nii-il06-published-figures.l4)
GIVEN h              IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the children` IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      x              IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the count of a parent excluded by section 66`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the child allowance for the month, in` h `, for the children section 72 pays for` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` `, reading the count of an excluded parent as` x MEANS
    CONSIDER `the child allowance of each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, reading` (`IL-06: its readings, with the count of an excluded parent read as` x)
                 `, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the month, in` `the family`
    WHEN LEFT  p             THEN `IL-06: the refusal for` p
    WHEN RIGHT `the answers` THEN `the family's total, before rounding, of` `the answers`
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS `IL-06: the family in the month, in` h `, with the children section 72 pays for` `the children` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`

@ref NII s 67 (row IL-06 v0.4.0, nii-s67-count-of-children.l4, its fork F6)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      x IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the count of a parent excluded by section 66`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the number of children in the earner's count, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax` `, reading the count of an excluded parent as` x MEANS
    count (`s 67 — the count of children, reading` (`IL-06: its readings, with the count of an excluded parent read as` x) `, in` `the family`
               `, of` (`IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`))
    WHERE
        `the family` MEANS `IL-06: the family on the first day of the month, in` h `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`

@ref NII s 66 (row IL-06, nii-s66-entitlement.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `chargeable to additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-06: the earner is an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax, in` h `:` `chargeable to additional tax` MEANS
    `s 66 — an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax` (`IL-06: the earner as a person, in` h `, with income chargeable to additional tax:` `chargeable to additional tax`)

§§ `Figures IL-06 sourced from the National Insurance Institute (not law)`

@ref [nii-basic] (row IL-06, nii-il06-published-figures.l4)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the basic amount under paragraph (2)(a) in force on` `the day` MEANS
    (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` `the day`)'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`

@ref [nii-basic] (row IL-06, nii-il06-published-figures.l4)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-06: the basic amount under paragraph (2)(b) in force on` `the day` MEANS
    (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` `the day`)'s `under paragraph (2)(b)`
